BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:a272bc9f-4fac-4ad3-8027-752ae47d0efb
DTSTAMP:20260223T193042Z
DTSTART:20260226T180000Z
DTEND:20260226T193000Z
SUMMARY:Free Food @ Creative Practice Lab: Lunch Day with Artist Dario Robleto
DESCRIPTION:Join us at University Galleries for the inaugural semester of the Creative Practice Lab (CPL)! Socialize with other students and arts professionals; participate in professional development activities; and help shape future semesters of the group. Free food at all meetings and free to participate. Register for each event at: https://linktr.ee/universitygalleriesisu     At this event, lunch with internationally recognized artist Dario Robleto. Join other students and University Galleries’ team for a casual lunch and conversation with the artist. Robleto will be in town for a film screening on February 24 and lecture on February 25.     **Registration is limited to 20 currently enrolled ISU students. The registration form will be closed once capacity has been reached. If you have any questions, please contact Gallery@IllinoisState.edu.
LOCATION:University Galleries
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:a3c29bb3-f58f-4d36-8c1d-a64e3cf9e0d1
DTSTAMP:20260223T193042Z
DTSTART:20260226T233000Z
DTEND:20260227T023000Z
SUMMARY:Free Food/Stuff @ Dinner &  A Movie : Wicked: For Good
DESCRIPTION:Enjoy dinner, a backstage tour of Braden Auditorium, and Wicked: For Good!  Limit 150 participants. Admission is first come, first serve. No RSVP required. RSVP does not guarantee participation.  Doors Open & Optional Tour of Braden Auditorium Backstage: 5:30 p.m.  Dinner Served & Movie Begins: 6 P.M.  Menu: Baked Potato Bar  If you need accommodation to fully participate in this program/event, please contact Event Management, Dining, and Hospitality at 309-438-8351 or EMDH@IllinoisState.edu. Please allow sufficient time to arrange the accommodation.
LOCATION:Braden Auditorium, Bone Student Center
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:5a396838-2afa-421d-bc59-0bb791a44519
DTSTAMP:20260223T193042Z
DTSTART:20260227T180000Z
DTEND:20260227T190000Z
SUMMARY:Free Food @ Conversations Café
DESCRIPTION:Conversations Café 🕛 12:00 – 1:00 PM 📍 OIE Lobby, 2nd Floor Fell Hall  Join us for the Conversations Café, a cozy, coffee shop–style gathering hosted by the OIE I-House and Academic Teams. This program offers a welcoming space for students to connect, unwind, and engage in global conversations.  Enjoy: ✅ Coffee, tea, and snacks from a featured country ✅ Board games and friendly, global conversations ✅ A craft table and stress-relief activities ✅ A calm, inclusive atmosphere  Whether you want to practice your English, learn about different cultures, meet new people, or take a break from a busy week, this is the perfect place to relax and recharge.  All students are welcome—no RSVP necessary!
LOCATION:Fell Hall, Second Floor Lobby
END:VEVENT
